# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# KCD 60x2 gameplay, 5.2 min recorded locally on the release policy, b:vsync -src 60 -lock -lag 75 -etw -dejit 2026-09-23 (first VS2026 build, 9bb20a5); loading and exit trimmed. Lock pull wraps with no stall anywhere in the window
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD 60x2 gameplay, 5.2 min recorded locally on the release policy, b:vsync -src 60 -lock -lag 75 -etw -dejit 2026-09-23 (first VS2026 build, 9bb20a5); loading and exit trimmed. Lock pull wraps with no stall anywhere in the window
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 47
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.6
field_pull_wraps 3
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: the lock wrap on its own. The pull is held in [0, comb) with a band of comb/16
# (1041 us) either side; from about 42 s to 135 s of this log it sat within about 1 ms of the
# wrap point and crossed the band's edge four times, wrapping a whole comb each time: a repeat
# at 43.08 s (inside the replay's warmup, so not counted), a skip at 104.36 s, a repeat at
# 118.95 s and a skip at 124.65 s. There is no hold, no stall and no capture gap anywhere in the
# window, so each wrap is the only thing happening at its present, and the repeats and skips
# cancel: they are avoidable in principle. Each one is on screen in the local recording at
# frame precision (log = video + 43.68 s; the repeat at 118.95 s is the still frame at video
# 75.27 s, found by eye before anything else was known).
#
# WINDOW. KCD loads into gameplay with capture stalls of up to 1.7 s until log 42.4 s, and the
# exit starts at 357.4 s. Cut 42.5 s to 357 s: every relay hold, blocked present and capture gap
# over 50 ms in the log falls outside it.
#
# FIDELITY. Replay 0.8% / runs 0 / worst 47 / pull wraps 3 against field 0.6% / runs 0 / worst
# 47 / pull wraps 3; the dejitter arm, which is how the relay ran, reads 0.6% / 0 / 47, exact.
# Each replayed wrap lands within one present of the field's. That holds
# only at the capture's own lag: replayed without the 75 ms of extra lag, the pull sits half a
# source period away and none of the three wraps happens.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. max_pull_wraps is the one this fixture is for: a fix for the wrap lowers it.
# It read 3 on the comb/16 band; with the band above the comb at comb/8 it reads 1, and the
# bound holds that.
max_worst_run 47
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.2
min_reseeds 0
max_pull_wraps 1
src_hint 60.0
extra_lag_ms 75
